{"overview":"Two fast-talking insurance salesmen meet Mary, who is running away from her wealthy mother, and they agree to help her run a hotel that she owns. When they find out that the hotel is run down and nearly abandoned, they launch a phony PR campaign that presents the hotel as a resort favored by the rich. Their advertising succeeds too well, and many complications soon arise.","tagline":"Riding a Cyclone of Laughs Through a Broadway Hotel","cast":[{"n":"Bert Wheeler","c":"Wilbur Boswell","p":"/bgMgv0WuE58zuw9BGEQmXljm9Qj.jpg","q":"Q4895372"},{"n":"Robert Woolsey","c":"Addington Ganzy","p":"/3MvDnbu1ILAKPg6WV1dqpOpQucM.jpg","q":"Q326679"},{"n":"Dorothy Lee","c":"Mary Marsh","p":"/lcyXyRoZTVgN9IkuMKjsGW7uttA.jpg","q":"Q4353386"},{"n":"Jobyna Howland","c":"Mrs. Rebecca Marsh","p":"/aYLj5qXSboEirMnrf5r9kQuallu.jpg","q":"Q3179812"},{"n":"Natalie Moorhead","c":"Duchess Bessie Von Essie","p":"/cLtXMbNHcIiyg3hlfCJl7chHuPh.jpg","q":"Q1793030"},{"n":"Hugh Herbert","c":"Hotel House Detective","p":"/zEEjBlC4cPhn1xWN84eJ13dDJyR.jpg","q":"Q613705"},{"n":"George F. Marion","c":"Ritz de la Rivera Bellboy","p":"/bJ1rF0A1UkH8mgjR6925qIY2wW7.jpg","q":"Q3760487"},{"n":"William B. Davidson","c":"Frank Dukette aka Duke of Winchester (as","p":"/20RHbZvvujZFlR2B96i7oQaJ6w.jpg","q":"Q3568402"},{"n":"Stanley Fields","c":"McKay, Blackwell Henchman","p":"/tSPmFJbUooLXafkhmUkuqozHBT7.jpg","q":"Q3968233"},{"n":"Ralf Harolde","c":"John Blackwell aka Buffalo Blackie","p":"/3SphHINjbpRSzw7zhVYeKVvfo4T.jpg","q":"Q15069921"}],"country":["United States"],"language":["English"],"wiki":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hook,_Line_and_Sinker_(1930_film)","qid":"Q5897808","rel":{"US":{"d":"1930-12-26"}},"backdrops":["/1P7VK3k3Vq6bz2UXeyg1lDM1b7r.jpg"]}